segments.source:
Now we row reduce, noting that the second row is <m>i</m> times the first:
          <me>
            \mat{-i -1; 1 -i}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_2=R_2-iR_1}\;
            \mat{-i -1; 0 0}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_1=R_1\div -i}\;
            \mat{1 -i; 0 0}.
          </me>

segments.translation:
이제 둘째 행이 첫째 행의 <m>i</m>배임에 주목하여 행 축약을 합니다. <me>
            \mat{-i -1; 1 -i}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_2=R_2-iR_1}\;
            \mat{-i -1; 0 0}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_1=R_1\div -i}\;
            \mat{1 -i; 0 0}.
          </me>

segments.source:
Now we row reduce, noting that the second row is <m>-i</m> times the first:
          <me>
            \mat{i -1; 1 i}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_2=R_2+iR_1}\;
            \mat{i -1; 0 0}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_1=R_1\div i}\;
            \mat{1 i; 0 0}.
          </me>

segments.translation:
이제 둘째 행이 첫째 행의 <m>-i</m>배임에 주목하여 행 축약을 합니다. <me>
            \mat{i -1; 1 i}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_2=R_2+iR_1}\;
            \mat{i -1; 0 0}
            \;\xrightarrow{R_1=R_1\div i}\;
            \mat{1 i; 0 0}.
          </me>

답을 다음과 같이 검증할 수 있습니다. <me>
            \begin{split}
            \mat{1 -1; 1 1}\vec{i 1} \amp= \vec{i-1 i+1} = (1+i)\vec{i 1} \\
            \mat{1 -1; 1 1}\vec{-i 1} \amp= \vec{-i-1 -i+1} = (1-i)\vec{-i 1}.
            \end{split}
          </me>

segments.source:
We row reduce, noting that the second row is <m>-i</m> times the first:
          <me>
            \begin{split}
            \mat{i 1 0; 1 -i 0; 1 2 \frac{6-3i}5}
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_2=R_2+iR_1}\;
            \mat{i 1 0; 0 0 0; 1 2 \frac{6-3i}5} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_3=R_3+iR_1}\;
            \mat{i 1 0; 0 0 0; 0 2+i \frac{6-3i}5} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_2\longleftrightarrow R_3}\;
            \mat{i 1 0; 0 2+i \frac{6-3i}5; 0 0 0} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{\tiny\hss$R_2=R_2\div (2+i)$\hss}]{R_1=R_1\div i}\;
            \mat{1 -i 0; 0 1 \frac{9-12i}{25}; 0 0 0} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_1=R_1+iR_2}\;
            \mat{1 0 \frac{12+9i}{25}; 0 1 \frac{9-12i}{25}; 0 0 0}.
          \end{split}
          </me>
          The free variable is <m>z</m>; the parametric form of the solution is
          <me>
            \syseq{
            x = -\dfrac{12+9i}{25}z;
            y = -\dfrac{9-12i}{25}z\rlap.
            }
          </me>
          Taking <m>z=25</m> gives the eigenvector
          <me>v_2 = \vec{-12-9i -9+12i 25}.</me>

segments.translation:
둘째 행이 첫째 행의 <m>-i</m>배임에 주목하여 행 축약을 합니다. <me>
            \begin{split}
            \mat{i 1 0; 1 -i 0; 1 2 \frac{6-3i}5}
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_2=R_2+iR_1}\;
            \mat{i 1 0; 0 0 0; 1 2 \frac{6-3i}5} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_3=R_3+iR_1}\;
            \mat{i 1 0; 0 0 0; 0 2+i \frac{6-3i}5} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_2\longleftrightarrow R_3}\;
            \mat{i 1 0; 0 2+i \frac{6-3i}5; 0 0 0} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{\tiny\hss$R_2=R_2\div (2+i)$\hss}]{R_1=R_1\div i}\;
            \mat{1 -i 0; 0 1 \frac{9-12i}{25}; 0 0 0} \\
            \amp\;\xrightarrow[\hbox to 2cm{}]{R_1=R_1+iR_2}\;
            \mat{1 0 \frac{12+9i}{25}; 0 1 \frac{9-12i}{25}; 0 0 0}.
          \end{split}
          </me> 자유변수는 <m>z</m>이고, 해의 매개변수 꼴은 다음과 같습니다. <me>
            \syseq{
            x = -\dfrac{12+9i}{25}z;
            y = -\dfrac{9-12i}{25}z\rlap.
            }
          </me> <m>z=25</m>로 두면 다음 고유벡터를 얻습니다. <me>v_2 = \vec{-12-9i -9+12i 25}.</me>

segments.source:
In the first example, we notice that
      <me>
        \begin{split}
        1+i \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_1 = \vec{i 1} \\
        1-i \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_2 = \vec{-i 1}.
        \end{split}
      </me>
      In the second example,
      <me>
        \begin{split}
        \frac{4+3i}5 \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_1 = \vec{-12-9i -9+12i 25} \\
        \frac{4-3i}5 \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_2 = \vec{-12+9i -9-12i 25}
        \end{split}
      </me>
      In these cases, an eigenvector for the conjugate eigenvalue is simply the <em>conjugate eigenvector</em> (the eigenvector obtained by conjugating each entry of the first eigenvector).

segments.translation:
첫 번째 예에서는 다음을 알 수 있습니다. <me>
        \begin{split}
        1+i \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_1 = \vec{i 1} \\
        1-i \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_2 = \vec{-i 1}.
        \end{split}
      </me> 두 번째 예에서는 다음과 같습니다. <me>
        \begin{split}
        \frac{4+3i}5 \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_1 = \vec{-12-9i -9+12i 25} \\
        \frac{4-3i}5 \text{ has an eigenvector }
        \amp v_2 = \vec{-12+9i -9-12i 25}
        \end{split}
      </me> 이 경우들에서 켤레 고윳값에 대한 고유벡터는 바로 <em>켤레 고유벡터</em>(첫 번째 고유벡터의 각 성분에 켤레를 취하여 얻은 고유벡터)입니다.

그러면 <me>
          A - \lambda I_2 = \mat{z w; \star, \star}
          \quad\implies\quad
          \vec{-w z}
          \text{ is an eigenvector with eigenvalue } \lambda,
        </me> 위 벡터는 해당 고윳값에 대한 고유벡터입니다. 단, <m>A-\lambda I_2</m>의 첫 행이 0이 아니라고 가정합니다.

segments.source:
The rotation angle <m>\theta</m> is the counterclockwise angle from the positive <m>x</m>-axis to the vector <m>{a\choose b}</m>:
              <latex-code mode="bare">
                \usetikzlibrary{angles}
              </latex-code>
              <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-.5) -- (0,2);
  \draw[vector] (0, 0) -- (-2, 1) node[above] {$\vec{a b}$};
  \coordinate (v) at (-2,1);
  \coordinate (o) at (0,0);
  \coordinate (x) at (1,0);
  \pic[draw, ->, angle radius=.5cm, angle eccentricity=.5] {angle=x--o--v};
  \node at (.5, .5) {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
              </latex-code>

segments.translation:
회전각 <m>\theta</m>는 양의 <m>x</m>축에서 벡터 <m>{a\choose b}</m>까지 반시계 방향으로 잰 각입니다: <latex-code mode="bare">
                \usetikzlibrary{angles}
              </latex-code> <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-.5) -- (0,2);
  \draw[vector] (0, 0) -- (-2, 1) node[above] {$\vec{a b}$};
  \coordinate (v) at (-2,1);
  \coordinate (o) at (0,0);
  \coordinate (x) at (1,0);
  \pic[draw, ->, angle radius=.5cm, angle eccentricity=.5] {angle=x--o--v};
  \node at (.5, .5) {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
              </latex-code>

segments.source:
Therefore, it has the form <m>(\cos\theta,\sin\theta)</m>, where <m>\theta</m> is the counterclockwise angle from the positive <m>x</m>-axis to the vector <m>{a/r\choose b/r}</m>, or since it is on the same line, to <m>{a\choose b}</m>:
              <latex-code mode="bare">
                \usetikzlibrary{angles}
              </latex-code>
          <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-.5) -- (0,2);
  \draw[help lines, rotate=-10] (1, 0) arc[radius=1, start angle=0, delta angle=200];
  \draw[vector] (0, 0) -- (-2, 1) node[above] {$\vec{a b}$};
  \point (B) at ({-2/sqrt(5)}, {1/sqrt(5)});
  \coordinate (v) at (-2,1);
  \coordinate (o) at (0,0);
  \coordinate (x) at (1,0);
  \pic[draw, ->, angle radius=.5cm, angle eccentricity=.5] {angle=x--o--v};
  \node at (.5, .5) {$\theta$};
  \node[left, inner xsep=1pt] (A) at (-1.5, .3) {$(a/r, b/r)$};
  \draw[thin, shorten >=1pt] (A.east) -- (B);
  \node[right] at (1.75, 1.25)
    {$\vec{a/r b/r} = \vec{\cos\theta, \sin\theta}$.};
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>
          It follows that
          <me>
            A = r\mat{a/r -b/r; b/r a/r}
            = \mat{r 0; 0 r}\mat{\cos\theta, -\sin\theta; \sin\theta, \cos\theta},
          </me>
          as desired.

segments.translation:
따라서 이 점은 <m>(\cos\theta,\sin\theta)</m> 꼴이며, 여기서 <m>\theta</m>는 양의 <m>x</m>축에서 벡터 <m>{a/r\choose b/r}</m>까지, 또는 같은 직선 위에 있으므로 <m>{a\choose b}</m>까지 반시계 방향으로 잰 각입니다: <latex-code mode="bare">
                \usetikzlibrary{angles}
              </latex-code> <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-.5) -- (0,2);
  \draw[help lines, rotate=-10] (1, 0) arc[radius=1, start angle=0, delta angle=200];
  \draw[vector] (0, 0) -- (-2, 1) node[above] {$\vec{a b}$};
  \point (B) at ({-2/sqrt(5)}, {1/sqrt(5)});
  \coordinate (v) at (-2,1);
  \coordinate (o) at (0,0);
  \coordinate (x) at (1,0);
  \pic[draw, ->, angle radius=.5cm, angle eccentricity=.5] {angle=x--o--v};
  \node at (.5, .5) {$\theta$};
  \node[left, inner xsep=1pt] (A) at (-1.5, .3) {$(a/r, b/r)$};
  \draw[thin, shorten >=1pt] (A.east) -- (B);
  \node[right] at (1.75, 1.25)
    {$\vec{a/r b/r} = \vec{\cos\theta, \sin\theta}$.};
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code> 따라서 원하는 대로 <me>
            A = r\mat{a/r -b/r; b/r a/r}
            = \mat{r 0; 0 r}\mat{\cos\theta, -\sin\theta; \sin\theta, \cos\theta},
          </me>가 성립합니다.

행렬 <me>
            A = \mat{1 -1; 1 1}
          </me>는 기하학적으로 어떤 일을 합니까?

segments.source:
Therefore, it scales by a factor of <m>\sqrt{\det(A)} = \sqrt 2</m> and rotates counterclockwise by <m>45^\circ</m>:
          <latex-code mode="bare">
            \usetikzlibrary{angles}
          </latex-code>
          <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[->] (-.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-.5) -- (0,2);
  \coordinate (v) at (1,1);
  \draw[vector] (0, 0) -- (v) node[right] {$\vec{1 1}$};
  \coordinate (o) at (0,0);
  \coordinate (x) at (1,0);
  \pic[draw, ->, "$45^\circ$", angle radius=1cm, angle eccentricity=.67] {angle=x--o--v};
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>
          Here is a picture of <m>A</m>:
          <latex-code>
\def\theo{\includegraphics[width=3.7cm]{theo5.jpg}}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1.3]
  \begin{scope}
    \clip (0,0) circle[radius=1];
    \node[circle, scale=1/sqrt(2)] (theo1) at (0,0) {\theo};
  \end{scope}

  \begin{scope}[opacity=.6, black!95]
    \draw[->] (-1.3,0) -- (1.3,0) node[coordinate] (l) {};
    \draw[->] (0,-1.3) -- (0,1.3);
  \end{scope}
  \draw[->,red] (1.1,0) arc[radius=1.1,start angle=0,delta angle=45];

  \begin{scope}[xshift=7cm]
    \begin{scope}
      \clip (0,0) circle[radius=sqrt(2)];
      \node[circle, rotate=45] (theo2) at (0,0) {\theo};
    \end{scope}

    \begin{scope}[opacity=.6, black!95]
      \draw[->] (-1.3,0) node[coordinate] (r) {} -- (1.3,0);
      \draw[->] (0,-1.3) -- (0,1.3);
    \end{scope}
  \end{scope}

  \draw[->, thick] ($(l)+(3mm,3mm)$) to[bend left]
    node[midway,above] {$A$}
    node[midway,below=.5cm,align=center]
    {rotate by $45^\circ$\\scale by $\sqrt 2$}
    ($(r)+(-3mm,3mm)$);

\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-code>
          An interactive figure is included below.

segments.translation:
따라서 이 행렬은 <m>\sqrt{\det(A)} = \sqrt 2</m>배만큼 확대하고 반시계 방향으로 <m>45^\circ</m>만큼 회전합니다: <latex-code mode="bare">
            \usetikzlibrary{angles}
          </latex-code> <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[->] (-.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-.5) -- (0,2);
  \coordinate (v) at (1,1);
